Rugby league the way it was played from 1908 to 1947: the foundation clubs of Sydney and Brisbane, the Northern Union, the Tests. Fast arcade footy, seven or thirteen a side, with a controller or the keyboard: against the computer at four levels, a mate on the same screen, or online. A stadium with a crowd that rises for the home side's tries, a season and finals, a league table, and a sheet of every match. By Fisher's Ghost Studios.

To run: Menu > Games > Foundation Footy

A controller is best (Xbox, PlayStation and Switch pads all work, as does the keyboard). Needs the 64-bit Raspberry Pi OS and a Raspberry Pi 5 (or 4). The game keeps itself up to date: it checks for a new build when it starts (Options > Game > Check for updates).
